take-back fine that was reduced to 600,000 euro after a November 24, 2022 settlement [TSLA_10K_2022-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000]. Earlier filings also disclose a February 2021 agreement to pay $275,000 to the EPA over Clean Air Act recordkeeping allegations [TSLA_10Q_2022-03-31__legal_proceedings__0000]. The risk factors add that Tesla is cooperating with government investigations, that no agency has concluded wrongdoing occurred, and that a 2018 SEC settlement involving a $20 million civil penalty remains in force [TSLA_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0037].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "TSLA", "company": "Tesla Inc", "findings": [{"point": "The fiscal 2025 10-K (ended December 31, 2025) Item 3 refers readers to Note 13, Commitments and Contingencies, for material pending legal proceedings, but that note's content is not in the context.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2025-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The California waste segregation investigation was ongoing in the fiscal 2023 10-K (ended December 31, 2023) and was settled by stipulated judgment in February 2024 with about $1.5 million in civil penalties and fees (Q1 fiscal 2024, ended March 31, 2024).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2023-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000", "TSLA_10Q_2024-03-31__legal_proceedings__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The German Umweltbundesamt fine on battery take-back obligations went from 12 million euro to 1.45 million euro and then to 600,000 euro after a settlement following a November 24, 2022 hearing (fiscal 2022, ended December 31, 2022).", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2022-12-31__legal_proceedings__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The fiscal 2022 10-K (ended December 31, 2022) risk factors describe the 2018 SEC settlement ($20 million civil penalty, board governance changes) and warn of further enforcement if compliance lapses.", "citations": ["TSLA_10K_2022-12-31__risk_factors__0037"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"col